// of one of its branches runs (agentrepl.v1.CreateWorkspaceAsyncMerge).
//
// THE FILE IS READ AT EVERY DEPLOY, never cached, so an edit takes effect on
// the next deploy without a daemon restart. The daemon converts the YAML to
// JSON and decodes it into DeployConfig with unknown fields REFUSED: a
// misspelled key is a refused deploy with the key named, never a silent
// default. Keys are the field names below in snake_case.
//
// A REPOSITORY WITHOUT THE FILE HAS NO DEPLOY. `workspace finished` and an
// async merge in it are refused, naming the file; there is no default
// destination.
//
// A DEPLOY RUNS THREE STAGES, IN ORDER, all inside the repository's queue, one
// deploy at a time:
//
//   pre_deploy   its hooks, then the built-in local merge when configured;
//                never held
//   deploy       one hook; the only thing a repository hold
//                (agentrepl.v1.UpdateDeployHold) skips
//   post_deploy  its hooks, in order; never held
//
// and then the daemon's own last steps, which no config changes: the report to
// an async merge's requester, closing the deploy's OWNER (the finished
// workspace, or the async merge's hidden merge workspace) and removing its
// worktree. A deploy whose hook fails FAILS: its owner is not closed, and the
// failure is handed back to the workspace that follows it, which is prompted to
